{
  "requirement": "The `Markdown` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Markdown;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Markdown;\nimpl Debug for Markdown;\nimpl Default for Markdown;\nimpl OutlineLang for Markdown;\nimpl Copy for Markdown;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.Markdown`**\n1. `Markdown` is a public unit struct.\n2. It implements `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `Copy` and `OutlineLang`.\n3. As an `OutlineLang`, it supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the Markdown chapter. The refining requirements `...markdown.language`, `...markdown.sections` and `...markdown.fingerprints` own the detail of those rules. This requirement only needs the type to supply them.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` and its helper `fn[check]` run against `languages::Markdown`.\n  - **Extensions:** the test uses the file name `a.MARKDOWN`. It asserts `extensions()` equals `[\"md\",\"markdown\"]`. It also builds a file name from each claimed extension in upper case and checks that it infers Markdown and selects `section[Check]`.\n  - **Fingerprint:** it asserts `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `markdown-structural-v1`. It also asserts that the inferred and explicit contents have equal fingerprints and that the content's scheme matches.\n  - **Outline and selection:** it asserts that the raw `outline()` selectors and spans match the explicit and inferred `OutlineContent`. It also asserts that `select(\"section[Check]\")` succeeds.\n  - **Structural search:** it runs `search_structure` and checks the returned ranges.\n  - **Trait impls:** the generic bounds `OutlineLang + Default + Copy` mean the test only compiles if `Markdown` implements them. The test also calls `Clone::clone` and `L::default()`. It asserts the type is zero-sized.\n- `outline_content.rs#fn[markdown_heading_levels_resolve_encoded_duplicates_and_anonymous_items]` tests Markdown selection rules in depth. It covers:\n  - heading nesting;\n  - percent-encoded titles;\n  - duplicate `#n` suffixes;\n  - an anonymous preamble section;\n  - a setext heading;\n  - a block item;\n  - spans and the shared outline.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc and compares the struct declaration with the book. Its `check_declaration` helper asserts the expected trait implementations equal `rustdoc.trait_impls(page)`. That check covers the listed `Debug` impl, which the other tests do not exercise. It also compiles the Habeas consumer against the SDK.\n\nNo obligation is left untested. Both Markdown tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.\n\nThe public-API test shells out to `cargo`. I treated it as adequate evidence for the declaration and trait list because it asserts equality.\n\nThe detailed rule behaviour belongs to the refining requirements and needs no further test here.",
  "references": "9ef0c8911840c467e4e65dbb7029f6363ff5df1ddc1e1d9d8b8ae99c4f4cd391",
